{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Thanks, Morgan. I need to report a significant safety concern. Since Monday, I've verified three selection errors involving the 1 mg/mL and 2 mg/mL anticoagulant concentrations. These errors occurred at the point of selection from the automated dispensing cabinets, where both concentrations are currently stocked side by side. Given the risk of a patient receiving the wrong concentration — which could lead to a serious dosing error with an intravenous anticoagulant — I'd recommend that pharmacy remove the bedside stock of both concentrations from the ADCs and supply only pharmacy-prepared 1 mg/mL syringes during a temporary hold. This would eliminate the selection risk at the cabinet level while we work through the safety review."}
```

