{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Morgan. To answer your question about patients currently on the protocol — I don't have specific information about which patients are currently receiving the anticoagulant or when they started therapy. What I can confirm is that the laboratory's approved replacement monitoring pathway, aPTT every six hours, is ready to support any patients on the protocol starting now and through Friday at 17:00 when the anti-Xa analyzer becomes available for calibration. From a laboratory operations standpoint, we can handle the aPTT monitoring volume without issue. One consideration I'd flag for the group: aPTT-based monitoring requires clinical teams to be aware that the therapeutic range and interpretation differ from anti-Xa-based monitoring, so clear communication of the monitoring plan to treating clinicians will be important. I don't have any additional concerns beyond what I've already reported regarding the analyzer and the approved replacement protocol."}
